<title>SPAIN: Endesa sees sales, profits boost from Enersis.</title>
<headline>Endesa sees sales, profits boost from Enersis.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish utility Endesa gave details on Friday  of the expected boost in sales and profits of its $1.5 billion purchase  of a controlling stake in Chilean power investment firm Enersis.</p>
<p>In a study using 1996 results as a model, Endesa said the deal would  have boosted attributable profit by 19 percent in that year to 197  billion pesetas (versus 165 billion as reported), and increased gearing  to 42.6 percent (versus 37.8 percent).</p>
<p>If the deal had taken place in 1996, sales in GW/h would have increased  by 20 percent, while customers would have increased by 24 percent.  1996 asset levels would have been boosted by 33 percent, according  to Endesa.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
